# Inexact literal element conversion rejected while compiling

Verifies a literal element the declared element type cannot represent is
rejected at compile time: `5mm` divided into whole centimeters has no exact
integer value, so `int<cm>[]` cannot store it.

>>> source
let sizes: int<cm>[] = [5mm]

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `int64[mm]` cannot be represented as `int64[cm]` at Span { start: 24, end: 27 }

<<< exit
1
